dsv41 patch 0076 (22.10.2026): head-node memory without functional change. In use from image v24 (VLLM_INDEXER_PREFILL_BUFFER_FACTOR=4 VLLM_DSV41_DROP_MTP_BUFFER=1 VLLM_EXL3_TF_PROMPT_TRANSIENT=1 VLLM_EXL3_TF_PROMPT_ALIAS=1).

Base: image v22 (model.py/model_runner.py = gh_stage v22, tf_prompt.py/tf_experts.py = image v4 = src_v12).
All switches default off = v22 bit for bit.

0076a VLLM_DSV41_MEMPROBE=<prefix> (+ _LAYERS="2,14,20", _MIN_TOKENS, _MAX): per-worker JSONL of torch allocated /
      reserved / peak per step, MemAvailable / RSS / AnonPages / SUnreclaim, per-phase peaks (attn / ffn / engram) of
      chosen layers in big eager steps, Engram reader time per step (engram_disk spin_stats). Measurement windows only.
0076b VLLM_DSV41_DROP_MTP_BUFFER=1: no [max_num_batched_tokens, hc_mult*hidden] bf16 MTP residual buffer for the DSpark
      drafter (written every forward, never read: dflash propose() takes combine_hidden_states(cat(aux)) whenever aux
      states exist). -160 MiB a rank at MAX_BATCH 4096 (-320 at 8192). Runner falls back to the plain hidden states.
0076d VLLM_EXL3_TF_PROMPT_TRANSIENT=1: TensorFold prompt scratch (xg/xu/xd/z: 1,014 MiB a rank at 4096 rows, kept for
      the whole run today) allocated per MoE call (torch.empty, call size) and released after it, so the other phases'
      temporaries reuse it instead of stacking on top. Same kernels, same arguments, same bits.
0076e VLLM_EXL3_TF_PROMPT_ALIAS=1 (with 0076d): the down's per-slot partials ([P, D] fp32) live in the storage of the
      gate/up rotated rows (2 x [P, D] fp16, dead after the gate/up launch); gate/up sums get [2, P, I] fp32.
      A call's peak 1,014 -> 750 MiB at 4096 rows. Same bits.
Config only (no code): VLLM_INDEXER_PREFILL_BUFFER_FACTOR=4 (0033's 8 holds 2x what max_num_seqs=4 seats at full length
      can gather; 4 changes no chunk split): indexer K-gather workspace 553 -> 277 MB a rank at MAX_LEN 524288.
Tests: loops/kopfspeicher/test_kopfspeicher.py, test_tf_transient.py (CPU, Mac).

Measured (22.10.2026, image v23, B1 factor 4 + 0076b + 0076d + 0076e, A/B on adjacent fresh starts):
  - T=0 8/8 identical; decode +0.03 % (geometric mean, worst cell -1.3 %) against v22 under the same clock;
  - lowest free memory on the head node under a 478K-token needle 2,493 -> 3,306 MiB (+813 MiB); after start
    +714 MiB (first window); prefill unchanged;
  - this is what makes max-model-len 1,048,576 fit: needle at 948,731 tokens 3/3 in 484 s, lowest free memory
    2,048 / 2,348 MiB on the two nodes (without the switches the serve was killed at 1,333 MiB by our watchdog).

